-blank-
^yellow;Antithetical Arts: 1.5 second perfect block time.^white;
^yellow;Passivity, Parted: 5hp blocking power.^white;

''I love cheap whiskey!''

A swig of flammable oil right down yer noggin', then right back out at the would-be Assassin in a wave of flame.

^#D6DFFF;Use to drink, and spit out a short-ranged flame blast.^white;

''I was separated from my group when I stumbled upon another lone Floran. Felt like an eternity till I just started running at him with my bayonet. He spun his spear 'round but it was too late; Knife went deep into his chest. Saw eye-to-eye. Poor soul looked underfed, scrawny. A lot smaller than me. I gave him a final shot to the head.''
Outdated assault rifle used during the late-stages of the USCM-Floran War, chambered in 5.56x45mm STANAG-FEDERATSIYA.
^orange;The Lost: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY^reset;

---
Outdated assault rifle used during the late-stages of the USCM-Floran War, chambered in 5.56x45mm STANAG-FEDERATSIYA.
^orange;The Lost: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY^reset;

''We pushed ourselves beyond the boundaries of our bodies. We did not simply push ourselves to the limit. We went beyond. It wasn't that they had their flesh torn. It was that they had their souls torn out.''

^orange;Cold-Blooded: 220HP STABILITY | 80% DEF.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user. Cannot perfect-block.^white;

Sometimes pronounced ''Wolfak'' or cynically as ''Well, fuck''. This kit offers a lot of equipment to address the broadest range of conditions. Often part of long-term colonization efforts in hostile environments.

^green;- Restores 400 health/10s | Heal Delay: 2.75s | Immobile Time: 3s
^yellow;Removes ALL BLEEDING.^white;
^orange;- Heals Burn Wounds^white; | ^yellow;- Heals Bruising.^white;
^red;- Heals Blood Loss^white; | ^gray;- Heals Fractures.^white;

''If I were to pick up this cowering-plate, I would have to put down my second sword,'' a Scotsman thinks. ''And surely that is madness.''

^yellow;Knightly Demolitionist: 0.5s PARRY WINDOW | 5HP BLOCK.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;+50% fire damage resistance on wearer.^white;
^#D6DFFF;+30% explosive damage resistance on wearer.^reset;
^#orange;Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal heightened damage based on the speed of the user.^reset;

''Who are the Resigans? It's where the Alliance of Independent Systems were born. The United Systems were getting too big for their own good and opted to split the nation in half. It saved them, but it can only last so long.''

5.45x39mm Resigan Assault Rifle K-designation, variant 6. Accepts AK 5.45x39mm magazines.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

A tainted remnant of the Tyrant Judge, a fragmented avatar of the Great Yamaxanadu.
The Tyrant Judge, as she was so-called, was ultimately a disjointed personality created from the One True Yamaxanadu created to hold the tide of Abyssal forces from outright wiping worlds that had an excess of psychic potential. Tragically, her efforts would often be for naught as humanity would still find a way to worsen their own state through petty conflicts.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

The White Wolves seldom used Greatshields, reserving the heavier equipment for the protection and rescue of lone pups, and to push back against threats to whatever new home they've found among humans.

^#B24A5A;Abyss-Walker: +0.5% HP regeneration when equipped in either hand | 600hp blocking power.^white;  
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user.^white;

''Everyone always says they can fashion shit from junk from their mother's arse. That they can sooo easily do it. Yeah, so why don't you make it, huh? Fuckin' city-folk...''

^#688686;I SAID GET BACK: Heavy Knockback and Bleeding in every shot.^reset;
^#D6AF8B;Can only use custom Owl-Hunter Bolts.^reset;
^yellow;Heat Overcharging: Direct hits lower enemy attack power by 50%

An oval scutum shield that can be aimed to provide cover against primitive missiles (but not against contemporary rocket-propelled munitions). The first depictions of the scutum were by the Este culture in the 8th century BC, and subsequently spread to the Etruscans, Illyrians, Celts, and Italians.

^green;Attacking Testudo: Can be aimed | 100hp blocking power (npc).^white;  
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user.^white;

A dull remnant of the Ex-Cultist, a man who imbued himself with otherworldly powers for the sake of survival.

The Ex-Cultist was a rather unremarkable man on a personal level. He did not care for any specific goal and was mostly interested in just collecting shiny trinkets and killing off anyone who he considered was worthy of fighting in a duel, which was more of a spectacle than a life-threatening duel.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

''The strongest took the spoils, and we fell down at their shoes.''

^orange;Heretic: 0.75s PARRY WINDOW | 180HP STABILITY | 60% DEF.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;Full Force Forward!: +25% HIT CHANCE and ACCURACY with [EWS] guns whilst equipped in either hand.^white;
^red;New Age Movement: Energy regeneration crippled whilst equipped.^reset;

''Just a piece of wood. That's what those stupid Protectors in their armchairs typing away on their computers would say. They don't have to do what I do to survive.''

^orange;Hot-Blooded: 3500HP STABILITY | 40% DEF.^white;

^#D6DFFF;Shield Rush: Moving at mere running speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage and ^orange;STUN^#D6DFFF; based on the speed of the user. 2-second cooldown per stun.^white;

Ask any sorcerer, and they'll tell you that something must be used as a catalyst to channel otherworldly energies. While the particular ''rules'' are unclear, any item with personal or sentimental value should suffice. Such items could include common weapons like swords, spears, bows, and even firearms.
^red;Energy regeneration is crippled while the bow is equipped.^reset;
^yellow;Arcane Archery: Standard shots fire 3 split arrows at a consistent speed regardless of draw-length. Charged shots fire a singular, piercing, soul-arrow.^reset;

Named the Spaceport Emergency First Aid Kit, this medical kit is often loaded into spaceships and ground flitter vehicles as standard in adherence to laws established after the first Golden Trail wars. ^green;This kit offers all the required equipment in sterile, controlled environments^white;.
^green;- Restores 150 health/3s | Heal Delay: 1s | Immobile Time: 2s
^yellow;- Heals Bruising.^white;
^orange;- Heals Burn Wounds.^white;
^gray;- Heals Fractures.^white;

''Anything could be a weapon if you're creative enough. A shield, after all, is just a wooden board with some handles. No one thing is capable of fighting against our ingenuity.''

^orange;Table Stance: 1000HP STABILITY | 45% DEF.^white;

^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user. Cannot perfect-block.^white;

A fiery remnant of the Hell Raven, a noble spirit given a world in turmoil.

The Hell Raven was in truth not a human like her sworn knight nor a synthetic like her robotic cousin on the resistance's side, but a youkai whose raw power and changed ways enabled her to assume nobleship of a dying state. Whether she was successful or not still remains to be seen.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

A crude 'kit' consisting of nothing more than a box of matches and a lighter. Used in the most dire of situations: If you're bleeding out, you probably don't have the steady hands necessary to strike a match, so that's what the lighter is for. Just ignite a fistful of matches and stab it in the wound.

^green;- Immediately recovers Light, Medium, and Heavy Bleeding.^white;
^orange;- Causes Burn Wounds.^white;
^red;- Mobility hindered for 5 seconds.^reset;

^#EA3C0B;Point-Blank Shot: Shots at muzzle range deal heavy damage, as well as knocking the enemy and player back^reset; | ^yellow;Cannot hit targets beyond point-blank ranges.^reset;
^orange;HIT CHANCE replaced with CRIT CHANCE. CRIT Shots increase pellet DMG by 3x.^reset;
^#EA3C0B;Highwayman's Resourcefulness: Shots are packed with large consistent pellets, dealing 5x50 additional damage | Auto-reloading.^reset;
Uses 20mm Musket Ball and Shot.

A bow compatible with standard Protectorate energy systems. Scales with the attack power of the user. Oni are not exactly something one would expect the Florans to fear, but that shouldn't be a problem with the advent of firearms...
^red;Energy Systems Overload: Energy regeneration is crippled whilst the bow is equipped.^reset;
^yellow;Lightning Puncture: When fully charged, fire a slow lightning arrow that flies perfectly straight, piercing all targets. Hit targets are stunned for a second.^reset;

A dull remnant of Maku, the synthetic woman.
Maku was built foremost as a personal idol for the growing resistance movement across a Protected world, and less so to serve any military purpose. She knew this from the moment she was ''born'', and dissociated herself from the questionable men who approved her assembly. To the agreement of a few commanders, she was given a quiet position along the resistance-held coast to live in peace.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

''The uniform. The maple-leaf emblem you have earned. Will make the difference between the freedom of the world, and its' enslavement.''

^#B24A5A;Abyss-Walker: +0.5% HP regeneration when equipped in either hand | 240HP STABILITY | 65% DEF.^white;  

^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user.^white;

The center of the shield features a large, sharpened spike which can be used to impale opponents when moving at great speeds. This shield was intended for a friend, but sometimes family just never arrive...
^yellow;Unbreakable Stance: 1.5s PARRY WINDOW | 5HP STABILITY.^white;
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user. More effective than Greatshields.
^red;Heavy Lance: 0.75s shield cooldown^white;

^#EA3C0B;Point-Blank Shot: Shots at muzzle range deal heavy damage, as well as knocking the enemy and player back^reset; | ^yellow;Cannot hit targets beyond point-blank ranges.^reset;
^orange;Brigand's Blast: Shots are packed with large pellets, dealing 5x50 additional damage.^reset;
Single-shot blackpowder weapon with immense firepower. Best used at point-blank ranges, for silencing foes too close for comfort. ^yellow;Immediately discarded after firing. A brace may assist with rapid-fire options...^reset;

A neutral remnant of the Occultist Assassin, a mercenary augmented by magic neither dark nor divine, but something given unto him by a loving patron.
For some, magic was a pathway towards degeneracy and a sign of a failing humanity. For others like the Occultists, they would embrace these new ideas and integrate them into their work. After all, if a rat swarm could bring down an enemy target just as well as a concealed blade, why not take the option?
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

Liquid medicine concocted by the occult scholars of the United Systems. Their unending search for wonder-weapons leads them to windows that should've never been looked-through, and doors that should've never been open.
^yellow;Does not stack with the World Walker artifacts, which will^reset; replace ^yellow;this medicine's effect.^reset;  
^green;Immunity to Suspicious Sensations for 6 hours.^reset;

^#8FAED3;Attunes the wand to explode, dealing significant damage to anything within a massive radius.^reset;

^red;The bearer and any nearby allies are not immune to this, and will most likely die in the process.^reset;

''The Dynasty must survive. It's just a pleasant bonus if it keeps us alive.''

A flickering remnant of the Greenfinger General, a Drufloran soldier who held the line alone while others fled.
The Greenfinger General served as a retainer for his Daimyo, having been adopted after said Daimyo's forces were ordered to execute his own parents. Despite holding the high ranking of Samurai, he yearned for something more than total dominion over mere peasants and knew that one day, he would face a worthy adversary.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

''The skies have burnt above. Mankind has abandoned us.''

^#D6DFFF;Unmoving Posture: 2.0s PARRY WINDOW | 200HP STABILITY | 50% DEF.^white;

^red;Accursed Attacks: -50% GENERAL RESISTANCE when equipped in either hand.^white;

An oval scutum shield that can be aimed to provide cover against primitive missiles (but not against contemporary rocket-propelled munitions). The first depictions of the scutum were by the Este culture in the 8th century BC, and subsequently spread to the Etruscans, Illyrians, Celts, and Italians.

^green;Attacking Testudo: Can be aimed | 100hp blocking power (npc).^white;  
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Moving at great speeds and colliding with an enemy will deal damage based on the speed of the user.^white;

''I told you to cease fire. Are you supposed to be observing? I see you with a goddamned rifle!''

A stripped-down and shortened version of the USM47. At the onset of the Floran Invasions, only a handful of colonies were properly-equipped to fight a war.
^orange;Vandal: Alt-fire to utilize attached bayonet.^reset;

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a questionable one-handed stance.^reset;

'Paket Bystrogo Vosstanovleniya' or 'Quick Recovery Package' is a mass-producible medical kit intended to quickly recover life-threatening damage in a combat environment using traditional methods: The equipment within this kit contains a significant amount of hemotherapy paraphernalia.
^green;- Restores 100 health/4s | Heal Delay: 0.75s | Immobile Time: 1.5s
^yellow;- Heals Bruising.^white;
^red;- Heals Blood Loss.^white;
^gray;- Heals Fractures.^white;

Heroin is made when morphine is heated and combined with certain chemicals. One of the biggest differences between heroin and morphine is the tripled potency. Its impure chemical composition makes it unsuitable for use in medical crafting.
^green;- Restores 50 health/1s | Heal Delay: 1.25s | Immobile Time: 1.75s
^yellow;- Heals Bruising.^white;
^red;- Causes Opiate Addiction.^white;

An energetic remnant of Legion, the Erchius Commander who would assemble an army.
When the Coordinator overrode the defense systems of the area, the renegade mind would need a force capable of directly assaulting the colony itself to drive out its human occupants. Legion represented that answer; ruthless in its march, an army of stone soldiers marched with spears forwards and with a curious sense of historical affinity.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

A fading remnant of the False Protector, an abomination who hid under the skin of a long-dead Shell.

The Abyss uses any means necessary to bring its corruption into the world. Whoever was under that lie has long since died, leaving only a malevolent force to wreak its havoc as much as it can. What its' goals were, none can say.

^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

A tainted remnant of the Eye of the Satori.
The Satori were a race of youkai who were simply able to read the thoughts of humans. When extensive strategic nuclear bombing campaigns wreaked its havoc across Europe during the Third World War, the Gensokyan Barrier broke and they were able to see firsthand the wants and desires of a dying humanity. As fractured spirits, some would attempt to safeguard nuclear facilities from any future prying eyes.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

The lord of the Japanese island Tanegashima Tokitaka (1528-1579) purchased two matchlock rifles from the Portuguese and put a swordsmith to work copying the matchlock barrel and firing mechanism.

Uses 20mm Blackpowder Ball and Shot ammunition.

^#DD765F;HIT CHANCE replaced with CRIT CHANCE (all projectiles always hit). CRIT Shots have different effects based on the shot.^reset;

''My days of hunting down Protectors ended when I finally ran out of shot on the battlefield.''

Multi-shot blackpowder weapon with immense firepower. Uses 20mm Blackpowder Ball & Shot ammunition.
^green;Will always hit at point-blank ranges.^reset;
^red;Cannot hit targets beyond point-blank ranges.^reset;

Also known as the ''Double-Arc'' shield, this type of shield was the most ubiquitous ''Chinese'' shield. It could be made of lacquered hide mounted on a wooden frame, lacquered wooden plank, or wood with lacquered hide facing. Many of the intricate shields still used by the Dynasty are handed-down from previous generations, kept immaculate via mundane and magical means.
^orange;Dead Empire: Cannot parry | 280HP STABILITY | 65% DEF.^reset;
^#D6DFFF;Shield Bash: Deals damage based on the speed of the user | +100% Knockback Resistance^white;

''This place was once full of guns like this. To the Protectors, it may seem like a mystery as to how the Insurgents were able to turn the tide of the war so quickly. Best not to dwell on that.''
Koloniya's early solution to the rifle power gap. Boasting 7.7x56mm ammunition, the CCR71 is capable of penetrating walls (along with most other mid-caliber weapons like the Lewis Gun) at long-distances and runs off the logic that more energy means more damage. Loads STANAG-K 7.7x56mm Magazines
^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''I was separated from my group when I stumbled upon another lone Floran. Felt like an eternity till I just started running at him with my bayonet. He spun his spear 'round but it was too late; Knife went deep into his chest. Saw eye-to-eye. Poor soul looked underfed, scrawny. A lot smaller than me. I gave him a final shot to the head.''
Outdated assault rifle used during the late-stages of the USCM-Floran War, chambered in 5.56x45mm STANAG-FEDERATSIYA.
^orange;The Lost: 0.6s PARRY WINDOW | 100HP STABILITY^reset;

A dull remnant of the Armored Protector, a knight who swore himself in service to the Hell Raven.

Much like other Immortal Shells, this unknown knight roamed human space in search of some challenge or adversary to face. After seeing the grace of a Hell Raven, he swore himself to her, if only to obtain some sort of purpose.

^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

A flaring, highly-infused remnant of Ruslan Stanislav, a man whose skill was entirely without magic, neither abyssal nor divine. He was weak by the standards of immortals, but by following his training he fought off someone far more powerful than he was.
Ruslan was a former member of the colonial government that predated the planet's apocalypse. Their uniform and training harkon heavily to the Great Soviet-era of pre-21st Century Earth.

^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

''Don't you dare go hollow!''

The Shells are immortal individuals who've been unceremoniously granted the powers of undeath. They they are undying, they often lose parts of their memories much in a similar capacity to alzheimers and dementia. Without purpose or reason after countless mortal deaths, they lose their sense of self. In a sense, they go ''hollow''.
^orange;Hollow Knight: 1.0s PARRY WINDOW | 160HP STABILITY | 65% DEF^reset;

The marking says the following:
^green;''This weapon is the only remnant of what it used to belong to Anson Sioux and later ^green;Major Tanya.''^white;

It is implied that this is a 'recreation' by an obsessed fan. Someone must've dedicated their lives over a show that they decided to make a functional firearm out of it, detail by detail. Props to whoever created did this.

A strong remnant of the Scatter-Spear Sicario, a human warrior on-par with those that would need magic to do his job.

The Sicario hunted down both Man and Youkai in the underground halls of subterranean colonies, taking jobs against targets that were suspected of involving otherworldly magic. Even if he was a hired gun, a sellsword, and a mercenary... He always kept his morals closer, for the hunt was more important.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

''Othniel's army will be upon us. We hold our shield wall here and we die standing.''

The Wolf-Tengu would stand over Youkai Mountain, guarding against an enemy that would never come. It would be Othniel who would test the strength of the Tengu after hundreds of years of peace and complacency.

^#D6DFFF;Unmoving Posture: 2.0s PARRY WINDOW | 200HP STABILITY | 95% DEF.^white;
^red;Accursed Body: -50% GENERAL RESISTANCE when equipped in either hand.^white;

''I was created for one purpose: Peace. I was instructed for one purpose: Peace. I was assigned for one purpose: War.''

An older-model energy shield that still used metal frames to contain a hardlight 'wall'. Rusted beyond repair, it's a wonder this item wasn't already scrapped.

^#D6DFFF;Rusting Hulks: 0.45s PARRY WINDOW | 0.25s COOLDOWN.^white;

''I've always been curious about why one man jumps out of a foxhole with a grenade and charges a machine gun nest, and his buddy next to him sits there cowering. And my feeling is that the difference is tiny between the two.''

Uses the unique MR-42 7.92x57mm Magazine.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''Empty though the space may be, there are a great many dangers between the stars. What makes these threats most dangerous is that they are few and far between, thus lulling the unwary traveler into complacency.''

Uses 7.62x39mm STANAG-USM Mags. Most models were built after 2659, marking the end of Floran invasions in human space.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

''Is that... my blood?''

The weapon is extraordinarily old and rusted with blood, degrading rapidly with each shot.

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to reload.^reset;
^#D6AF8B;Can only use Wooden Bolts.^reset;

''We're all sent here to kill Florans weren't we? What the hell difference does it make, what weapon we use!? I'll use my goddamned hands if I have to.''

A stripped-down and shortened version of the USM47. At the onset of the Floran Invasions, only a handful of colonies were properly-equipped to fight a war.

^green;Double-Tap [SHIFT] to switch to a comfortable two-handed grip.^reset;

''An arrow does not hate its target.''

^red;Energy Systems Overload: Energy regeneration is crippled whilst the bow is equipped.^reset;

^yellow;Fire Arrows: Regular shots coat afflicted targets in oil | Charged shots that are not overcharged apply ignition to oil granting heightened fire burning on oil-coated targets, but do not coat targets in oil.^reset;

-blank-

^yellow;Martial Warfare: 1.5 second perfect block time.^white;
^yellow;All or Nothing: 5hp blocking power.^white;

A flickering remnant of the Greenfinger Daimyo, a man who built an empire from ash.
The Daimyo poured everything into building a new Drufloran society built upon the ashes of an alien regime that died centuries ago. Learning from what little human curios still remained within their tribal archives, the Daimyo worked to accelerate his people in a new path; a direction that would not not be prone to the failings of the old ways.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

Large medicinal pellets, created from the blood of Youkai themselves. These were researched by Youkai Separatist alchemists before their project was cancelled due to Gensokyan Parliamentarian bombardments. These pellets are sometimes still concocted by the more feral youkai, who are more than willing to turn on their more 'civilized' kind to sustain themselves.
^#CE7777;Nearby enemies receive -50% DMG RES and Weapon Proficiency | Lasts 60s.^white;
^red;User is also afflicted with these effects.^white;

''An arrow does not hate its target.''

^red;Energy Systems Overload: Energy regeneration is crippled whilst the bow is equipped.^reset;

^yellow;Fire Arrows: Regular shots coat afflicted targets in oil | Charged shots that are not overcharged apply ignition to oil granting heightened fire burning on oil-coated targets, but do not coat targets in oil.^reset;

A partial remnant of the Wolf-Knights, a long-dead order of Tengu who sought to protect humanity against the Abyssal threat.

The Wolf-Knights were an ancient breed of Wolf-Tengu specifically tasked with protecting humanity from the Abyss. They were first employed within Gensokyo once signs of the Abyss began to reveal, marked by the Barrier's cracking at the start of World War 3 in 1991.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;

Some sort of healing flask. Only dropped by [GiC] Bosses.

^green;Heals 200hp in a second. All Bleeding is removed.^white;
^red;Mobility hindered for 1 second.^white;

''When the term 'machine gun' enters common parlance, the word 'machine' becomes much more sinister.''

Fires the heavy 11.43x23mm pistol cartridge using unique 30rnd MHP45 stick magazines. Supports receiver-type attachments.

^green;Hold down "Alt Fire" to switch between Full Auto and Semi-Auto.^reset;

^#E0C200;''-and death only brings death.''^reset;
^#E0C200;+30% Psychic Resistance^reset; for 1 hour.

^#52A8DD;Harried by years of brutal cold and plagued by visions of realms beyond, the Metro Wanderer has traversed their homeland as much as their own mind.^reset;

''Move! My mum's faster than you!''

A ^yellow;modern combat stimulant^white; issued to specific militaries of the ^green;United Systems.^white; While not technically chemically-addictive, many still feel as if they cannot operate without it.

^green;Grants suppression immunity^white; for ^yellow;2 hours.^white;

-blank-

^yellow;Force Deflection: 1.5 second perfect block time.^white;
^yellow;All-in: 5hp blocking power.^white;

A type of crossbow intended for use to face mobs alone, with immense suppressive power. When the lupine tengu became aware of the psychic cold, they were forced to fight the possessed townsfolk of their homelands.
^#688686;Gank Squad: Heavy Knockback in every shot.^white;
^red;Distant Scar: Heavy Bleeding in every shot.

An energetic remnant of Coordinator, a fragmented personality of a different mind.
The Coordinator was born from an Abyss-tainted fragment of the Erchius hive. Dredged from the depths, the Coordinator kept itself hidden from human excavations to bide its time and make plans for a takeover. When the time was right, it installed itself onto the colonial reactor, overriding the synth directives and overthrowing its human inhabitants.
^#FFE460;Trade at a Soulsmith to transform into something greater.^reset;
